      <h2>📍 Today's Watch List</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Westlake Town Council: when it votes on the Circle T settlement Keller approved Thursday.</li>
        <li>Hinojosa: the rest of her transition appointments, and whether any TCEQ or PUC nominees could win two-thirds of the Senate. She takes office Jan. 19, and the session opens Jan. 12.</li>
        <li>Abbott: whether he keeps, changes or lifts the TCEQ permit pause before he leaves office. Cantor expects permits to resume between mid-December and mid-January.</li>
        <li>Batch Zero complaints: lists of issues due Nov. 19 in Skybox's Docket 60431, with matching orders in Dockets 60356, 60396, 60410 and 60425. The complaints' pause runs until Nov. 10.</li>
        <li>Project 59999: comments and any public hearing requests on the standard large-load interconnection agreement are due Dec. 14.</li>
        <li>Today, Nov. 6: ERCOT's Medium Load RFI responses are due at 5 p.m., and SB 6 large-load curtailment workshop #2 runs 9:30 a.m. to noon.</li>
        <li>Agriculture Commissioner-elect Tucker's moratorium bill, and any data center bills filed for January.</li>
        <li>Hut 8: closing on the two West Texas Poolin sites, expected as early as the fourth quarter, and financing for Beacon Point Phase 2.</li>
        <li>Nscale: who signs for the rest of its Texas capacity.</li>
        <li>Oncor: its 2027–2031 capital plan, due in the first quarter of 2027, and how much Batch Zero load it includes.</li>
        <li>Docket 59399: Oncor and Comanche Peak filed again Thursday in the Comanche Peak–Amazon case.</li>
        <li>ERCOT will file its good-cause exception next week for loads that weren't energized by July 10, for the PUC's Dec. 17 meeting.</li>
        <li>Bastrop: whether the council acted on the 48-turbine Cedar Creek gas plant.</li>
        <li>Core Scientific's TCEQ enforcement case in Denton, and Denton's moratorium vote, as early as Dec. 1.</li>
        <li>Dallas: the Economic Development Committee's next meeting, when the deferred data center standards come back.</li>
        <li>ERCOT: Planning Working Group Nov. 9, System Planning Working Group Nov. 10, Batch/CTP workshops Nov. 17 and 19, TAC Nov. 18, Large Load Working Group and a PUC open meeting Nov. 19, another PUC meeting Dec. 3.</li>
        <li>ERCOT's final community impact report and audit reports are due Dec. 10, and Abbott's permit pause is tied to the audit. The PUC meets Dec. 17. Chevron's final investment decision on its West Texas Microsoft project is due by the end of 2026.</li>
      </ul>

